infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Why the dashboard took 4.6 s: serial tree vs hoisted parallel
  desc Same 23 widgets, same queries — only the await structure changes the wall-clock
  compares
    - label Serial staircase — the tree's default
      children
        - label 23 widgets, each awaits its own query
          desc Components nest, so each section awaits before its children render
        - label ~200 ms per step against us-east
          desc Nothing is slow; everything is sequential
        - label Total = the sum of every step
          desc 23 x ~200 ms stacks into a staircase of ~4.6 s to first byte
        - label Waterfall depth = nesting depth
          desc The component tree becomes the query planner, and it defaults to a waterfall
    - label Hoist + Promise.all or preload
      children
        - label Parent starts every promise at once
          desc Promise.all([getRevenue(), getErrors(), getCustomers()]), pass results down as props
        - label Total = the slowest query
          desc Wall-clock collapses from the sum to the max
        - label ~200 ms to first byte
          desc One step's latency instead of 23 stacked
        - label Preload: call early, await late
          desc void getOrder(id) shares the in-flight cache() promise; children join it
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
